# CODEOWNERS
#
# Code owners are automatically requested for review when a pull request
# modifies a file they own. Ownership is read from the CODEOWNERS file on
# the pull request's *target* branch.
#
# Reference:
# https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/managing-your-repositorys-settings-and-features/customizing-your-repository/about-code-owners
#
# Syntax: <path pattern>  <owner> [<owner> ...]
# Owners may be @users, @org/teams, or email addresses.
# The last matching pattern wins.
#
# Example — request a review from @<user> on every pull request targeting
# a branch that contains this file:
#
#   *  @<user>
#
# Note: this only *requests* a review; it does not block merging. To make
# owner approval mandatory, edit the branch ruleset (or branch protection
# rule) for the target branch and enable "Require review from Code Owners".
